---
/**
 * /check/ — the free instant check. THIS IS THE LEAD OFFER.
 *
 * It replaces Review Autopilot in that slot, which stopped being defensible in
 * March 2026 when a platform shipped that whole category free inside the tool
 * the buyer already opens daily.
 *
 * WHY A CALCULATOR AND NOT A DEMO. The seven industrial demos prove capability
 * and prove nothing about the VISITOR. This hands them a number about their own
 * business in under a minute, ungated, and the commerce lives inside the answer
 * rather than in front of it. That is the pattern the strongest sites aimed at
 * local owners use, and it is the only thing on this site that works on somebody
 * who has never heard of custom software.
 *
 * THE HONESTY CONTRACT is stated on the page and enforced in the island: every
 * figure is the visitor's own input through arithmetic printed beside it. No
 * model, no forecast, no benchmark. Same discipline as Confirmation Outlook's,
 * for the same reason — a claim nobody can check is worth less than no claim.
 */
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import CostCheck from '../components/CostCheck.jsx';
import IslandSkeleton from '../components/IslandSkeleton.astro';
import { startingPrice } from '../data/services';
---
<MarketingLayout
  title="What is the paperwork costing you?"
  description="A free check: two numbers in, one number back, with the arithmetic printed. No signup, nothing sent anywhere. Then a straight conversation about whether software is worth building."
  image="/og/default.png"
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-line">
    <div class="bg-grid bg-grid-fade pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 -z-10 opacity-60"></div>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-16 pb-10 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-14">
      <p class="mono-label">Free · no signup · nothing sent anywhere</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
        Find out what the paperwork is costing you.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Every business I have worked in had somebody doing the ordering by hand and nobody adding up
        what that was worth. Two numbers below and you will know — with the
        <span class="aiq-accent">arithmetic printed</span>, so you can check it yourself.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* The check itself, as high on the page as it can go. Nielsen's eye-tracking
      puts roughly 42% of all viewing time in the top fifth of a page, so
      anything between the headline and the first input is time spent on
      persuasion the tool would have done better. */}
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-10 sm:py-14">
    <CostCheck client:only="react">
      <IslandSkeleton slot="fallback" variant="chat" />
    </CostCheck>
  </section>

  {/* Everything below is for the visitor who has their number and wants to know
      what happens next. It is deliberately AFTER the tool, never before it. */}
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-16 sm:pb-24">
    <div class="border-t border-line pt-10">
      <p class="mono-label">What this is not</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
        No model, no forecast, no industry average.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Every figure above is one of your own numbers multiplied out, and the working is printed
        next to each line. Nothing is compared against a benchmark I cannot show you, and nothing
        you typed left your browser — there is no form here, and no email box.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        The number is not a promise about what software would save you. It is the size of the
        problem, which is the only honest thing a calculator can tell you. What a build would
        actually change depends on what gets built, and that is what the first conversation is for.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 border-t border-line pt-10">
      <p class="mono-label">And then</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
        A straight answer, then a fixed number.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        The first conversation is free and it can happen at your counter. If there is nothing worth
        building I will say so — that is a shorter conversation and it costs you nothing either way.
        If there is, {startingPrice.line.toLowerCase()} {startingPrice.qualifier}
      </p>
      {/* THE ASSESSMENT DOOR, added 2026-09-03, and this is the sharpest step on
          the site. A reader here has just watched their own numbers turn into an
          hours figure and has no way to tell WHICH of those hours is worth
          automating. That is the assessment's entire job.

          NOT ITS PRICE, ONLY A LINK. scripts/verify-assessment.mjs asserts that
          this page does not carry the assessment's price line, as a negative
          control proving the price is not simply everywhere. A link keeps that
          control meaningful. If a later change wants the figure here, that
          control gets REDESIGNED rather than deleted. */}
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        And if the number above is real but you cannot tell which part of it to fix first — that is
        what the <a href="/ai-fit/" class="link-sweep">AI Fit Assessment</a> is for. I come out, watch
        the work, and write the list in order.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <a href="/contact/?intent=consult" class="btn btn-primary">Start with a free conversation →</a>
        <a href="/work/" class="btn btn-secondary">See what I build</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
